iterations.reply:
The build failure was a naming issue: only the types listed in the world's `use` are generated at the crate root, so `ModeratedQuery`, `PolicyViolation`, and `EscalationRequest` now come from `crate::aap::caps::types`. I also changed unrecognised model replies to escalate instead of passing as OK.

I left out the operations team's two additions, the log-file append and the metadata fetch. This node's only capability is `LLMClient<inference>`. Writing a file would need a filesystem import, which `wasm32-unknown-unknown` without a WASI adapter doesn't have. Fetching would need `aap:caps/http-client` with that host in its allowlist. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond its graph declaration. It would also send the untrusted question text to another service. If operations wants these, the graph needs to grant the capabilities, for example a dedicated logging or enrichment node.

